      "message": "Maybe name like `SkFreeWrapper`? That does seem to be how it\u0027s written in the commit message. On the other hand, this is technically an `SkFreeDeleter` since the point is to use it as the `Deleter` template argument to `std::unique_ptr`. Though it does seem an odd name, since this is not for deleting `sk_free` but is a concrete instantiation of the `Deleter` concept / interface (though apparently it isn\u0027t spec\u0027ed as a Concept yet). On my third hand this is `SkFreeFunctionObject` since the actual \"C++ named requirement\" this is implementing is `FunctionObject`.\n\nUgh, naming things.",
      "revId": "8923612570a13f70482bd966313b68ab241eaa5c",
